cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FSSAI-RA: Fail-Secure Sovereign AI Reference Architecture"
message: "If you use this software, cite this software record and the exact commit used. Cite related papers separately when relevant; see publications/README.md in the repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Srivastava
    given-names: R.
repository-code: "https://github.com/genaiworks/fssai-ra"
url: "https://github.com/genaiworks/fssai-ra"
abstract: >-
  An extensible, runnable reference platform for specifying and testing the
  authority boundaries of agentic AI. It implements a seven-field control
  contract, bounded model checking of a governance profile's declared authority
  space, ablation-measured authority coverage, and a portable conformance suite
  so that replacing a backend does not silently void the assurance argument. It
  additionally verifies delegated authority across chains of agents, models
  human review as a finite resource whose ceiling moves but does not disappear
  when reviewers are given an AI assistant, and measures whether each contract
  requirement is bound to a check that runs or only to a sentence.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
license: Apache-2.0
